      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked in the Tint/WGSL room and they should have caught it if you didn\u0027t bind a 10001. File a bug against Dawn. Also, it\u0027s legal in Tint to assign any positive 32-bit number to a binding, but if Metal has tighter restrictions, Tint would need to fix it up somehow and apparently it is not; that\u0027s likely a second bug.",
